  clock: 4  # 5344
  nonce: '5344'  # 5344
  message: "DONE. PR #609, dev e18be75f3c. Measured A/B; write-up at\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/nular_f5_ab_08282026/RESULT.md\n\n26 rows moved net_recv -> net_send: Phoenix.Controller.{render, json, text,\nhtml, redirect, send_resp, send_download, put_status}; Plug.Conn.{send_resp,\nsend_file, send_chunked, chunk, resp, put_resp_header, put_resp_content_type,\nput_resp_cookie}; Phoenix.Channel.{push, broadcast, broadcast!, broadcast_from,\nbroadcast_from!, reply}; Phoenix.Endpoint.{broadcast, broadcast!,\nbroadcast_from, broadcast_from!}. Plug.Conn.halt REMOVED (moves no bytes either\nway). Plug.Conn.{read_body, fetch_query_params, fetch_cookies} KEPT as receives.\n\nTHE ROUTER DSL IS DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED. Phoenix.Router.{get, post, resources,\nscope, ...} declare where a request ARRIVES and arrival has no call site, so\nthey are the Django shape from WI-hikut and the JS-createServer shape from\nWI-dosov: moving them would relocate the receive to nothing.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, canary NEW 26 / OLD 0 Phoenix-Plug net_send rows:\n  net_recv chains  53 -> 14   net_send chains  20 -> 58\n  phoenix-framework alone     0 -> 18 net_send chains\n  all 10 other boundaries     IDENTICAL\nThe -39/+38 is attributed PRIMITIVE BY PRIMITIVE: the four genuine receives\nstay, the nine senders move, and the one-row difference is `halt`.\n\nTHE FINDING THE OLD CATALOGUE COULD NOT PRODUCE. The standing claim file\nprohibits only host_fs sinks and therefore cannot see a network change at all --\nworth remembering, it is why my first extract showed no verdict movement. On a\nNETWORK claim: plausible UNTRUSTED-NO-NETWORK violated(4) -> violated(7), the\nthree new findings sinking at Phoenix.Controller.json -- untrusted input reaching\nan HTTP RESPONSE BODY. HOSTSECRET-NO-NETWORK holds at 13 as an in-run control\n(those reach the network through HTTP clients, always rowed).\nphoenix-framework stays inconclusive, correctly: it is the framework library,\nnot an application, so it has no request handlers of its own.\n\nDIRECTION: unlike the other INV-nular families this REPORTS MORE. It adds sinks;\nthe removals it performs delete false sources. Both halves move away from the\nall-clear, which is why it needed less evidence than F1-F4, not more.\n\nNOT CLAIMED: two repositories is a demonstration, not a rate. Nothing here\nre-measures 0006."  # 5344
